#: source/protocols/nix32.md:1
msgid "Nix32 Encoding"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:3
msgid ""
"Nix32 is Nix's variant of [Base32](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base32) "
"encoding, used for [store path digests](../protocols/store-path.md), hash "
"output via [`nix hash`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-hash.md), and the "
"[`outputHash`](../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-outputHash) "
"derivation attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:5
msgid "Alphabet"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:7
msgid "The Nix32 alphabet consists of these 32 characters:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:13
msgid "The letters `e`, `o`, `u`, and `t` are omitted."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:15
msgid "Byte Order"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:17
msgid ""
"Nix32 encoding processes the hash bytes from the end (last byte first), "
"while base-16 encoding processes from the beginning (first byte first)."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/nix32.md:19
msgid ""
"Consequently, the string sort order is determined primarily by the first "
"bytes for base-16, and by the last bytes for Nix32."
msgstr ""
